  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>Place the pumps</b> on the island at local x = \u22122.0 and x = +2.0, standing on the curb."
--- !u!114 &-520269328521491573
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>The pump</b> is a prefab (<i>Prefabs/Fuel-Pump.prefab</i>, 1.0 \xD7 2.0 \xD7 0.56 m). It is built once and placed twice: a change to the prefab changes both pumps. Look inside it in Prefab Mode: a plinth, two posts, a lower panel, a meter housing, a top cap, and on each face a screen, a price display, a keypad and a nozzle in its holster. The hose is a separate mesh (<i>Meshes/Pump-Hose.asset</i>)."
